      messages: ["query", "declare_subscriber"],
      key_exprs: ["zk2/vehicle-01/thruster-l/**", "zk2/vehicle-01/thruster-l/*/@stream/**", "zk2/vehicle-01/thruster-l/*/@state/**", "zk2/vehicle-01/thruster-l/*/@op/**", "zk2/vehicle-01/thruster-l/@zk/**"] },
    // fan_in (vehicle-01/thruster-l): §11.2, §3.3 (0.27): the descriptor's GET and subscription ride the presence grant (0.14) and, unlike a liveliness read, travel toward the provider, which serves its descriptor: every presence selector that intersects this provider's `@zk` subtree, and that its own patterns do not include, is granted here. Without it a wildcard descriptor read, a doctor's or an inspecting tool's, is refused at the provider (measured, #748). No reply rule: a descriptor is a value reply, checked against its own key
    { id: "fan-in-presence:vehicle-01/thruster-l", permission: "allow", flows: ["egress"],
      messages: ["query", "declare_subscriber"],
